{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAQxxT5MoXLToqoLcsrD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `Hijack()` in `response_writer.go` so that sending only headers no longer blocks it. Before, it refused to hijack once anything was marked as written, including just the status line. WebSocket libraries send the `101 Switching Protocols` status and then hijack, so that flow broke. Now `Hijack()` returns `errHijackAlreadyWritten` only once body bytes have been written (`size > 0`).\n\nI added a test case to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite` that writes only the 101 header and then hijacks. The check script ran it twice: it failed without the fix and passed with it, and its format and leftover-debug checks were clean. The existing \"hijack after body write should fail\" case still passes.\n\nI only ran the hijack tests, not the full suite, and I didn't try it against a real WebSocket library."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1243,"cache_read_input_tokens":33565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1243,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8ff3155-aaf9-4378-8bd4-996e1c6bad52","uuid":"ebcd4229-c3dc-4bc1-bcd7-3cdca12f8bae","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:29:33.679Z","request_id":"req_011CgAQxxES2zLuUJZSiXrw8"}
